    h2 Usage

    h3 files structure
    code.src-js.source_visible
        ||--component/ folder ( component's main container )
        ||  |--templates/ folder
        ||  |  |--data/ folder
        ||  |  |  |--data.json / data file that you can use it as reference
        ||  |  |--component/ folder
        ||  |  |  |--component-tmpl.jade / template file
        ||  |--index.jade/ file used by sourcejs to represent components options and their html code
        ||  |--info.json/ data file used by sourcejs

    h3 json files structure
    markdown
        p We are compiling html code using json files by passing data and templates to `$pug`
    +printJson({"$pug": {
                   "template": "..",
                   "data": {

                   }
               }})
    markdown
        p include template file`"template": "full/path/to/component/templates/component/component-tmpl.jade"`
        p you can pass the data as json code using `"body": [{}]`
        p or passing the data from an external reference file using `"$ref": "path/to/data/file.json"`

    h3 Data structure
    +printJson({"config": {
                   "class": {
                       "addClassNames": ["class__name"]
                   },
                   "class": {
                       "useClassNames": ["class__name"]
                   }
               },
               "body": [
                   {
                       "data-elment": "value",
                   }
               ]})
    markdown
        p In `"config"` object we provide the css classes that will be used for different template components, either you add a class by passing the value to `"addClassNames"` so it will be added to the template default classes, or you override the default classes that is already declared in the template by passing the value to `"useClassNames"`
        p in `"data"` object we provide the actual data (static data for now) that will be used in the template, we define the `"data-elment"` set that can be used in each template inside the component page
    h3 Json file example
    p this is a real example of the heading component
    h4 passing data object
    +printJson({"$pug": {
                   "template": "./templates/headings/headings-tmpl.jade",
                   "data": {
                       "config": {
                           "level": "h2",
                           "class": {
                               "addClassNames": ["section__header"]
                           }
                       },
                       "body": [
                           {
                               "text": "Latest Articles"
                           }
                       ]
                   }
               }})
    h4 Send data as json file by using $ref reference to json file
    +printJson({"$pug": {
                   "template": "./templates/headings/headings-tmpl.jade",
                   "data": {
                       "config": {
                           "level": "h2",
                           "class": {
                               "addClassNames": ["section__header"]
                           }
                       },
                       "body": [
                           {
                                "$ref": "./templates/data/content.json"
                           }
                       ]
                   }
               }})


    h4 Widgets Json structre
    markdown
        p
            b note:
            | Widgets Json structre must start with `model` object
    +printJson({
        "$pug": {
            "template": "./widgets/most-x/templates/most-x/most-x-tmpl.jade",
            "data": {
                "model": {
                    "config": {
                        "level": "h2",
                        "class": {
                            "addClassNames": ["section__header"]
                        }
                    },
                    "data": {
                        "$ref": "./templates/data/content.json"
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    })
